Disclaimer: The liver failure is terminal and irreversible. Treatment is exclusively focused on clearing toxins from the brain to maintain wakefulness and draining fluid for breathing comfort.
Clinical Course: The ascites will aggressively reaccumulate. Encephalopathy will become progressively harder to manage.

SAFETY-NETTING ADVICE

Daughter: Ensure the lactulose is taken exactly as prescribed, even if the patient complains of the taste. The goal is multiple loose bowel movements per day to clear the brain toxins.

PATIENT EDUCATION

